From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koji Ishii <kojii@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:18:56 +0900
Subject: [m156][m157][m158][icu] Cap formatted digits and check range status

Cherry-pick upstream ICU-23144 (commit 7964695d9f4b) and ICU-23539
(commit 11e6fff63958) into third_party/icu.

Guard writeNumber(), writeIntegerDigits(), and writeFractionDigits()
against magnitudes exceeding 999,999 digits so formatting fails
immediately with U_ILLEGAL_ARGUMENT_ERROR, and return early in
formatRange() when number formatting or string insertion fails before
applying modifiers.

Bug: 579234520, 579235238, 579235720, 567827593
Test: intltest format/NumberTest
Change-Id: I2d9b394a331755ea92c01e04ab90ee42bd9a406a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/deps/icu/+/8668341
Reviewed-by: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
(cherry picked from commit f338a36b97f0324d780ff63e6be5198391907a5a)
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/deps/icu/+/8723642

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
The upstream change also refreshes the copies of these fixes stored under third_party/icu/patches/ (number_max_digits.patch, numrange_impl.patch), which are only consulted when ICU is re-rolled and whose diff-context lines carry trailing whitespace that Electron's patch lint rejects; those stored-patch hunks are not carried. The ICU source and test changes are carried verbatim.

